6 0 obj
<< /Length 1060 >>
stream
BT
/F1 14.00 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 750.40 Tm (3.2 Multi-Leader Replication) Tj
/F1 10.00 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 736.40 Tm (Multiple nodes accept writes, which suits multi-datacenter deployment and clients that work offline.) Tj
/F1 10.00 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 722.40 Tm (The hard part is write conflict: the same row may be modified concurrently on two leaders.) Tj
/F1 10.00 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 708.40 Tm (Common fixes are last-write-wins, version vectors and application level merging of conflict-free data.) Tj
/F1 10.00 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 694.40 Tm (Last-write-wins is simple but silently discards data, so it is a poor default for financial records.) Tj
/F1 10.00 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 680.40 Tm (Version vectors detect that two writes are concurrent instead of pretending that one of them is newer.) Tj
/F1 10.00 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 666.40 Tm (Application level merging works when the data type has a natural merge function such as a grow-only counter.) Tj
/F1 10.00 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 652.40 Tm (Causal ordering helps: a write that saw another write should never overwrite it without a merge decision.) Tj
ET
endstream
endobj
