8 0 obj
<< /Length 1066 >>
stream
BT
/F1 14.00 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 750.40 Tm (3.3 Leaderless and Quorum) Tj
/F1 10.00 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 736.40 Tm (There is no leader: clients write to several replicas and read repair fixes divergence after the fact.) Tj
/F1 10.00 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 722.40 Tm (When the read quorum R plus the write quorum W is greater than N, the read and write sets must intersect.) Tj
/F1 10.00 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 708.40 Tm (Dynamo style stores use this model and push conflict resolution to the client application.) Tj
/F1 10.00 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 694.40 Tm (Anti-entropy repair scans replicas in the background and reconciles missing writes with a Merkle tree.) Tj
/F1 10.00 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 680.40 Tm (Hinted handoff keeps availability during a temporary failure but delays convergence until the node returns.) Tj
/F1 10.00 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 666.40 Tm (Sloppy quorums trade strict overlap for availability, so a reader may need several rounds to see the newest value.) Tj
/F1 10.00 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 652.40 Tm (Tunable quorums let operators choose latency versus consistency for each workload independently.) Tj
ET
endstream
